  <section>
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>Just Baked Maine is a family-owned adult-use cannabis dispensary in downtown Lincoln, on the I-95 / ME-6 corridor in interior Penobscot County. Per the operator's own site, Just Baked is the only full-service adult-use cannabis shop in the Lincoln area — an important geographic distinction for residents and travelers in northern Maine who would otherwise have to drive to Bangor or Millinocket for legal cannabis.</p>
    <p>The operator is Square One Natural Relief (the parent company's email domain). The dispensary markets itself as a small-but-mighty operator emphasizing handcrafted, commercial-grade edibles as a quality differentiator from mass-market competitors.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Lincoln Location</h2>
    <p><strong>Address:</strong> 115 West Broadway, Unit 2B, Lincoln, ME 04457<br>
    <strong>Phone:</strong> (207) 403-9160<br>
    <strong>Hours:</strong> Monday through Saturday 10am-6pm · Sunday 10am-4pm</p>
    <p>Lincoln is a small Penobscot County town of approximately 5,200 residents in northern Maine. The town sits on the I-95 / ME-6 corridor — a key north-south route through northern Maine. West Broadway is the main commercial corridor in downtown Lincoln, with restaurants, retail, and other small businesses in the surrounding blocks.</p>
    <p>Parking is available on-site and in nearby public lots. The dispensary is a short drive from I-95 exit 229 (Lincoln / East Millinocket).</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Product Specialization</h2>
    <p>Per the operator's own site, Just Baked carries:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Flower</strong> — multiple cultivars, indoor and outdoor</li>
      <li><strong>Pre-rolls</strong> — single joints and multi-packs</li>
      <li><strong>Handcrafted edibles</strong> — the operator's signature category, marketed as "a higher quality alternative to your standard gummies and cookies"</li>
      <li><strong>Vapes / Cartridges</strong> — 510-thread carts and disposables</li>
      <li><strong>CBD products</strong> — broad-spectrum and isolate formats</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Confirm current menu, pricing, and product availability with the operator before visiting — the menu rotates with each cultivation cycle.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Service Area</h2>
    <p>Just Baked serves the I-95 / ME-6 corridor in interior Penobscot County:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Lincoln</strong> (in town) — 5 min</li>
      <li><strong>Lee / Winn</strong> — 10-15 min</li>
      <li><strong>Mattawamkeag</strong> — 15 min</li>
      <li><strong>Howland / Enfield</strong> — 25-30 min south</li>
      <li><strong>Millinocket</strong> — 40 min north</li>
      <li><strong>Bangor</strong> — 50 min south</li>
      <li><strong>Houlton</strong> — 90 min north</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Just Baked is the only full-service adult-use cannabis shop in the Lincoln area, making it a critical access point for residents of interior Penobscot County and travelers on the I-95 corridor. The next-closest adult-use options are in Bangor (50 min south) and Millinocket (40 min north) for any products Just Baked does not carry.</p>
  </section>

